export const koreaPanel="<aside id=\"korea-sidebar\" class=\"sidebar korea-sidebar\" hidden aria-label=\"Explore Korea\"><div class=\"sidebar-tools\"><label class=\"sr-only\" for=\"k-search\">Find a place</label><div class=\"search-wrap\"><input id=\"k-search\" type=\"search\" placeholder=\"Find a place · 지역 검색\" autocomplete=\"off\" data-nav disabled></div><div id=\"k-search-results\" hidden></div><div class=\"panel-tabs\"><button id=\"k-tab-explore\" aria-pressed=\"false\" hidden>Discover</button><button id=\"k-tab-layers\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Map settings</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"sidebar-scroll\"><section id=\"k-layers-panel\"><label class=\"field-label\" for=\"k-country\">Scope</label><select id=\"k-country\" data-nav disabled><option value=\"\">All Korea</option><option value=\"KP\">North Korea · 조선</option><option value=\"KR\">South Korea · 대한민국</option></select><label class=\"field-label\" for=\"k-province\">Region</label><select id=\"k-province\" data-nav disabled><option value=\"\">All regions</option></select><section class=\"layers\"><h3>Visible layers</h3><label><span><i class=\"line province-line\"></i>Provinces &amp; special cities</span><input id=\"k-province-layer\" type=\"checkbox\" checked data-nav disabled></label><label><span><i class=\"line prefecture-line\"></i>Cities, counties &amp; districts</span><input id=\"k-prefecture-layer\" type=\"checkbox\" checked data-nav disabled></label><label><span><i class=\"label-icon\">Aa</i>Region names</span><input id=\"k-label-layer\" type=\"checkbox\" checked data-nav disabled></label></section><p class=\"coverage-note\">South Korea: July 2026 boundaries.<br>North Korea: OpenStreetMap snapshot.</p></section>\n<section id=\"k-explore-panel\" hidden><section id=\"k-selection\" aria-live=\"polite\"><div class=\"selection-top\"><button id=\"k-selection-reset\" class=\"back-button\" data-nav>All Korea</button><img id=\"k-selection-flag\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" alt=\"\"></div><span id=\"k-selection-kind\" class=\"eyebrow\"></span><h2 id=\"k-selection-name\" lang=\"en\"></h2><p id=\"k-selection-chinese\" class=\"korean-name\" lang=\"ko\"></p><p id=\"k-selection-country\"></p><div id=\"k-selection-meta\" class=\"selection-meta\"></div><div id=\"k-parent-context\" class=\"parent-context\" hidden><span class=\"name-caption\">Parent region</span><button id=\"k-parent-region\" class=\"quiet-button\" data-nav><span id=\"k-parent-english\"></span><span id=\"k-parent-chinese\" lang=\"ko\"></span></button></div><details id=\"k-subdivisions\" open><summary id=\"k-subdivisions-title\">Subdivisions</summary><div id=\"k-region-list\"></div></details></section></section></div>\n<footer class=\"sidebar-footer\"><button id=\"k-about-open\">Sources &amp; coverage</button><span class=\"creator-credit\">Created by Ethan Hu</span></footer></aside><dialog id=\"k-about\"><div class=\"dialog-head\"><button id=\"k-about-close\" aria-label=\"Close sources\">×</button></div><h2>Sources and coverage</h2><p>South Korea uses <a href=\"https://github.com/vuski/admdongkor/tree/master/ver20260701\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">vuski/admdongkor, July 2026</a>. This data is derived from administrative-dong boundaries released by <a href=\"https://sgis.kostat.go.kr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Statistics Korea SGIS</a> under KOGL Type 1, modified by vuski/admdongkor, distributed under CC BY 4.0.</p><p>Districts within ordinary cities are combined into their parent cities. Autonomous metropolitan districts remain separate. Sejong has no second-level division. Jeju’s two administrative cities are included. The July 2026 snapshot includes the Jeonnam–Gwangju merger.</p><p>North Korea uses <a href=\"https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/192734\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">OpenStreetMap administrative relations</a>, clipped to OpenStreetMap coastlines. © OpenStreetMap contributors, <a href=\"https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ODbL 1.0</a>. These are mapped boundaries; recent changes may not yet be represented.</p><p>Coastline vertices are retained without simplification. Province outlines are derived from the same subdivision geometry. English names use OpenStreetMap and the <a href=\"https://github.com/southkorea/southkorea-maps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">South Korea maps dataset</a>. Flags: flag-icons (MIT).</p><a href=\"data/korea-sources.json\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Source dates, processing and checksums</a><p><a href=\"data/korea-boundaries.bin\" download>Download map data (gzip JSON)</a></p></dialog>";
